    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Run vocal/instrument sound separation.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Target segment id (required; raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --mode TEXT         Track to keep: vocal / instrument\r\n          --keep TEXT         Track to keep, e.g. vocal / background\r\n          --sounds TEXT       Comma-separated instrument sounds\r\n          --apply TEXT        Apply mode: remove / keep\r\n          --output-dir TEXT   Directory for separated audio products\r\n          --format TEXT       Separated audio format\r\n          --production-path TEXT \r\n                              Existing separated audio product path\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Sound-separation timeout; explicit unit required (us, ms, s, min)\r\n          --poll-interval <duration> \r\n                              Sound-separation poll interval; explicit unit required (us, ms,\r\n                              s, min)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Keep only the vocal track\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo sound-separation --mode vocal --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Keep only the instrument track\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo sound-separation --mode instrument --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Select instrument stems and how to apply them\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo sound-separation --mode instrument --sounds drum,guitar --apply remove --seg-id <UUID>\r\n",
